   "stem": {
      "text": "The graphs of the functions f and g shown each consist of three line segments on \\( 0 \\le x \\le 6 \\). Let \\( h(x) = f(g(x)) \\). Find the exact value of \\( h'(1) \\).",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         7,
         2
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "By the chain rule, \\( h'(1) = f'(g(1)) \\cdot g'(1) \\). From the graph, \\( g(1) = 5 \\), and the segment of g through x = 1 has slope \\( g'(1) = -1 \\).",
         "rule_named": "read the inner value and slope"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The outer slope is read at the inner output x = 5, not at x = 1: the segment of f there has slope \\( f'(5) = - \\frac{7}{2} \\).",
         "rule_named": "read the outer slope at the inner output"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "So \\( h'(1) = \\left(- \\frac{7}{2}\\right) \\cdot \\left(-1\\right) = \\frac{7}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            7,
            2
         ],
         "rule_named": "chain rule"
      }
   ],
